# Rename session

Under tmux 3.4, `C-e` should open a rename prompt for the selected live session
with its current name available for editing.

    :bins jj tmux cat

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', and 'cat' are available.

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "sesh; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 100 -y 10 (success)
    :pane ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

    :k alpha
    :k C-e
    :snap

```terminal
rename: alpha
  1/3 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
▌⬤ alpha                                                                                           ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

Accepting the edited name should keep the picker open and refresh its session
list with the new name.

    :t set-hook -g session-renamed "set-hook -gu session-renamed; wait-for -S renamed-session" (success)
    :k C-u renamed Enter
    :t wait-for renamed-session (success)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :snap

```terminal
session: renamed
  1/3 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
▌⬤ renamed                                                                                         ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

    :t has-session -t renamed (success)

